      "problem": "$(x-3y)({x}^{2}+4y)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3y)({x}^{2}+4y) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}+4y)-3y({x}^{2}+4y) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4xy-3{x}^{2}y-12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms.",
